plane loads of weapons from the us uk  and other nato members were sent to  ukraine in the weeks before the war  broke out a response to russia's  military buildup along the country's  border  and after russia launched its violent  invasion on february 24th  though shipments not only got bigger but  they started coming in from more and  more countries those countries who  had never supplied us with weapons are  now doing so here's how some of the  western weapons being used by ukrainian  forces work and why they're so valuable  on the battlefield  hundreds of american javelins have been  sent to ukraine over the past few weeks  known as tank killers javelins are  particularly useful in urban combat  because they're portable  they weigh about 50 pounds and they can  be fired from a gunner's shoulder they  have a range of 65 to 4 000 meters in  most operational conditions in other  words they can hit a target nearly two  and a half miles away  and javelin missiles have infrared  seekers which allow them to make  adjustments in the air in order to hit a  moving target  javelins have two modes of fire straight  on or top attack  when shooting in top attack the missile  fires in an arc to hit the top of a  target  that's particularly important for  ukrainian forces trying to defeat  russian tanks because the top of a tank  is where it's most vulnerable  furthermore javelins are considered fire  and forget weapons the gunner doesn't  have to guide the missile to the target  and can immediately seek cover or shoot  at something else  ukrainians are also destroying russian  tanks and other targets with thousands  of n-laws sent by the uk n-law stands  for new generation light anti-tank  weapon similar to javelins they're  portable and can be fired from the  shoulder in both direct and top attack  mode  but there are some key differences at 27  pounds an n-law is almost half the  weight of a javelin and its range is  much shorter 20 to 800 meters  and the weapon uses what's called  predicted line of sight meaning the  missile cannot make adjustments in the  air  even though it can't fire as far as the  javelin experts say that that short end  of the short range can be especially  useful in urban combat settings and they  say that n-laws are going to get more  and more important as russian forces  close in on ukrainian cities  [Music]  then there are american stingers which  can shoot down low-flying airplanes  helicopters and even drones  stingers weigh 35 pounds so they're also  portable their range is classified and  stingers use an infrared seeker to lock  onto flying targets allowing them to  adjust their flight path mid-air  stingers are considered to be highly  accurate  and so far experts say that they've  helped ukraine prevent russia from  dominating the airspace  that's important because as long as the  airspace is contested russia can't just  bomb that will or freely fly troops and  equipment around the battlefield  and then there are turkish drones known  as tb2s which ukraine initially received  in 2019. the ukrainian air force says  the drones are now being used to conduct  surveillance and strike russian assets  each drone can carry four laser-guided  munitions according to the company that  makes them the drone can stay in the air  for 27 hours and it can be flown by a  remote pilot as far as 185 miles away  because the drones can hover for such a  long time experts say that they help  ukrainian forces view the battlefield  and identify high-value targets  still experts say russia maintains a  strong advantage in manpower air power  and sophisticated weaponry  and that's why ukrainian president  volodimerzelinski has been appealing for  much more than anti-tank and  anti-aircraft weapons  if you found this video informative  subscribe to the channel for more  stories like this i'll see you next time  [Music]  you
 

